{"type":"data","nodes":[{"type":"data","data":[{"stars":1},1],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"sections":1},[2,8],{"title":3,"pages":4},"",[5],{"title":6,"slug":7},"Introduction","index",{"title":9,"pages":10},"berm",[11,14,17,20,23],{"title":12,"slug":13},"Overview","berm/overview",{"title":15,"slug":16},"Writing a Program","berm/writing-a-program",{"title":18,"slug":19},"The Manifest","berm/manifest",{"title":21,"slug":22},"Publishing a Program","berm/publishing",{"title":24,"slug":25},"Running the Service","berm/service"],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"slug":1,"title":2,"description":3,"toc":4,"html":18,"prev":19,"next":22},"berm/publishing","Publishing a Program","A program is one file, so it travels as one OCI layer with no tarball around it.",[5,9,12,15],{"depth":6,"id":7,"text":8},2,"the-artifact","The artifact",{"depth":6,"id":10,"text":11},"one-digest","One digest",{"depth":6,"id":13,"text":14},"what-deploy-refuses","What deploy refuses",{"depth":6,"id":16,"text":17},"from-a-workflow","From a workflow","\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># berm.toml, beside the program's Cargo.toml\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">name = \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"example\"\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">image = \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"ghcr.io/org/example\"\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">public = []\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">crab\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> deploy\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>crab deploy\u003C/code> builds the program and, against a host that pulls from a\nregistry, pushes the image to \u003Ccode>image\u003C/code> tagged with the crate's version and\ndeploys that reference. Against \u003Ccode>bermd\u003C/code> it sends the image itself, so \u003Ccode>bermd\u003C/code>\nnever talks to a registry, holds no credentials, and still restores from\n\u003Ccode>--root\u003C/code> on start without a network.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"the-artifact\">\u003Ca href=\"#the-artifact\">The artifact\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">{\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  \"schemaVersion\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">2\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  \"mediaType\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"application/vnd.oci.image.manifest.v1+json\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  \"artifactType\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"application/vnd.berm.program.v1\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  \"config\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: { \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"mediaType\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"application/vnd.berm.manifest.v1+json\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"digest\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"sha256:…\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> },\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  \"layers\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: [ { \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"mediaType\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"application/vnd.berm.program.v1\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"digest\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"sha256:…\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> } ]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>The config blob is the \u003Ca href=\"../manifest/\">\u003Ccode>.berm.abi\u003C/code>\u003C/a> section carried out of the\nimage byte for byte, so what a registry serves cannot disagree with what the image\nholds. The tools, their schemas and the README are one blob, and reading them\nnever means pulling the program.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>Nothing about the program is repeated in annotations. Only\n\u003Ccode>org.opencontainers.image.source\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>.revision\u003C/code> are set, from\n\u003Ccode>GITHUB_REPOSITORY\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>GITHUB_SHA\u003C/code> when a build has them, which is what makes\nGHCR show a package against its repository.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"one-digest\">\u003Ca href=\"#one-digest\">One digest\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>Because the layer is the image and nothing else, the layer's digest is sha256 of\nthe image — the same hash \u003Ccode>crab ls\u003C/code> reports, carrying the registry's \u003Ccode>sha256:\u003C/code>\nprefix:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">$ crab ls\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">NAME     DIGEST        TOOLS\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">fixture  222890c498ed  echo\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">$ shasum -a256 target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/fixture.wasm\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">222890c498ed28f4bf60670a223141489d9879020bd1890111b8c11ac79fa31d\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>A pulled image is checked against the digest the registry advertised before it\ngoes anywhere, so a registry that serves the wrong bytes is caught by the deploy\nrather than by the model.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"what-deploy-refuses\">\u003Ca href=\"#what-deploy-refuses\">What deploy refuses\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>crab deploy\u003C/code> reads the manifest out of the image before it uploads anything,\nwhich means a broken image is refused by whoever built it rather than at deploy\non someone else's machine. Reading it never runs the guest.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"from-a-workflow\">\u003Ca href=\"#from-a-workflow\">From a workflow\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>GITHUB_TOKEN\u003C/code> is the registry credential, and the deploy is two lines — there\nis no action to install.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">permissions\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">  packages\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">write\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">steps\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  - \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">crab context add cloud https://api.crabtalk.ai --token \"$KEY\" --org acme\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    env\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">      KEY\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">${{ secrets.CRABTALK_KEY }}\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  - \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">crab deploy --context cloud\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    env\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">      GITHUB_TOKEN\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>Locally, \u003Ccode>GITHUB_TOKEN=$(gh auth token)\u003C/code> does the same. \u003Ccode>~/.docker/config.json\u003C/code>\nis not read.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>BERM_REGISTRY_MIRRORS\u003C/code> reaches a registry at another address, as\n\u003Ccode>name=endpoint\u003C/code> pairs separated by commas. A host in a container pulls what was\npushed to \u003Ccode>localhost:5001\u003C/code> from \u003Ccode>http://registry:5000\u003C/code> with\n\u003Ccode>BERM_REGISTRY_MIRRORS=localhost:5001=http://registry:5000\u003C/code>.\u003C/p>",{"title":20,"slug":21},"The Manifest","berm/manifest",{"title":23,"slug":24},"Running the Service","berm/service"],"uses":{"params":["slug"]}}]}
